ays-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026-27 Week 12 College Football Playoff, bowl projections","description":"Our bowl gurus take a look at how the postseason picture shifted after Week 12.","published":"2026-11-23T12:28:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564492/2026-week-12-college-football-playoff-bowl-projections","type":"Story","byline":"Kyle Bonagura and Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Power Rankings: Chaos shifts top 25 in Week 12","description":"UCLA and Ohio State fell, and three teams joined the list. How did the top 25 change after a wild Week 12?","published":"2026-11-23T12:14:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50545207/2026-college-football-power-rankings-top-25-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Tennessee fined by SEC after fans throw golf balls on field","description":"Tennessee was fined $250,000 by the SEC after fans threw golf balls and mustard bottles onto the football field late during Saturday's win over LSU.","published":"2026-11-23T01:42:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50568028/tennessee-fined-sec-fans-throw-golf-balls-field","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Notre Dame loses safety Luke Talich to torn Achilles","description":"Notre Dame starting safety Luke Talich sustained a torn right Achilles tendon in Saturday's win against SMU, sources told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-22T23:15:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50566676/notre-dame-loses-safety-luke-talich-torn-achilles","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What Week 12's unexpected results mean for Rivalry Week and beyond","description":"After another chaotic weekend, we look at the playoff and conference races on the line with one game to go.","published":"2026-11-22T23:54:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50563018/week-12-results-rivalry-week","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 recruit AJ Randle Jr. flips from Miami to Notre Dame","description":"Notre Dame coach Marcus Freeman flipped Miami pledge AJ Randle Jr., ESPN's No. 9 outside linebacker in the 2027 recruiting class, to fill a late-cycle need.","published":"2026-11-22T22:48:18.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50565158/2027-recruit-aj-randle-jr-flips-miami-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Pac-12 reveals unique flex schedule for season's final week","description":"The Pac-12 announced its unique flex schedule for the final week of the regular season early Sunday morning.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564960/pac-12-reveals-unique-flex-schedule-season-final-week","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079420/treydez-green","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trey%27Dez_Green"},"pick":{"pick":19,"round":1,"team":"CAR","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Trey'Dez Green","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trey%27Dez_Green","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:21Z","intro":"Trey'Dez Green (born February 18, 2006) is an American college football tight end for the LSU Tigers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Green was born in Jackson, Louisiana. He attended East Feliciana High School in Jackson before transferring to Zachary High School in Zachary, Louisiana for his senior year. He played football and basketball in high school. In football, Green had 45 receptions for 864 yards with 11 touchdowns his junior year and 53 receptions for 960 yards with 12 touchdowns his senior year. He committed to play college football and college basketball at Louisiana State University (LSU)."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman at LSU in 2023, Green played both tight end and wide receiver. He played in all 13 games with two starts and had 13 receptions for 101 yards with four touchdowns. In basketball, he played in six games as a freshman and averaged 1.8 points and 1.7 rebounds."}]}}